WEBVTT

1
00:00:03.048 --> 00:00:16.212
Dr. Dolittle had to let the fish go.

2
00:00:16.232 --> 00:00:21.733
"I wanted to take him back to Puddleby," the doctor said, "but he is so much happier in

3
00:00:21.773 --> 00:00:23.174
his own water world."

4
00:00:23.874 --> 00:00:25.454
Everyone nodded in agreement.

5
00:00:26.255 --> 00:00:31.456
"Just look how beautiful and calm the waters are," sighed Charles.

6
00:00:32.152 --> 00:00:33.533
"Look at that silly bird!"

7
00:00:33.973 --> 00:00:35.474
Tommy stood up and pointed.

8
00:00:38.256 --> 00:00:42.058
A bird was coming toward them, but it couldn't seem to fly straight.

9
00:00:42.458 --> 00:00:45.580
Everyone except Polynesia laughed.

10
00:00:45.620 --> 00:00:49.743
"Dr. Dolittle," she said seriously, "I think it's Miranda."

11
00:00:49.763 --> 00:00:52.284
"Miranda?" exclaimed the doctor.

12
00:00:52.304 --> 00:00:53.945
"What is she doing here?"

13
00:00:54.525 --> 00:00:58.488
As the bird approached, they recognized the purple bird of paradise.

14
00:01:02.432 --> 00:01:05.735
"Oh," Miranda gasped as she fell onto the boat.

15
00:01:05.755 --> 00:01:08.257
"Miranda! Are you all right?"

16
00:01:08.658 --> 00:01:09.759
the doctor called out.

17
00:01:09.779 --> 00:01:12.281
"Yes," she finally said.

18
00:01:12.301 --> 00:01:14.783
"I was looking for you for weeks!

19
00:01:15.503 --> 00:01:17.906
But I couldn't find The Curlew anywhere!"

20
00:01:17.926 --> 00:01:23.150
"Yes, er, well we had to change boats," stammered the doctor.

21
00:01:23.170 --> 00:01:26.733
"I bring bad news," she continued.

22
00:01:26.753 --> 00:01:29.896
"A storm, a big storm, is coming."

23
00:01:30.612 --> 00:01:32.994
Tommy looked up at the clear sunny sky.

24
00:01:33.634 --> 00:01:36.156
It certainly didn't look as if a storm were coming.

25
00:01:36.176 --> 00:01:38.638
"It's not too late to turn back, Dr.

26
00:01:38.658 --> 00:01:40.299
Dolittle," Miranda said.

27
00:01:40.759 --> 00:01:42.080
The doctor shook his head.

28
00:01:44.161 --> 00:01:44.982
She tried again.

29
00:01:45.002 --> 00:01:46.603
"I wish you would."

30
00:01:46.623 --> 00:01:51.646
"We are going to Spider Monkey Island," the doctor said firmly.

31
00:01:51.666 --> 00:01:56.290
"Then be very careful, Doctor," she said sadly.

32
00:01:57.290 --> 00:01:59.552
Miranda shook her wings and flew away.

33
00:02:00.432 --> 00:02:03.234
Everyone watched her disappear into the blue sky.

34
00:02:06.316 --> 00:02:09.098
That night Miranda's words came true.

35
00:02:09.118 --> 00:02:11.100
"Tommy! Charles!

36
00:02:11.400 --> 00:02:11.880
Wake up!"

37
00:02:12.341 --> 00:02:14.782
Dr. Dolittle's voice sounded from the dark.

38
00:02:15.483 --> 00:02:16.944
Tommy turned the lamp on.

39
00:02:16.964 --> 00:02:18.625
"I need you on the deck!"

40
00:02:19.145 --> 00:02:20.546
the doctor said urgently.

41
00:02:20.566 --> 00:02:22.568
"The storm is here."

42
00:02:24.649 --> 00:02:28.212
Dr. Dolittle stood by the wheel trying to turn it to the right.

43
00:02:28.972 --> 00:02:31.374
But the wind kept pushing the boat to the left.

44
00:02:31.394 --> 00:02:33.956
"The sails," Dr.

45
00:02:33.996 --> 00:02:35.418
Dolittle shouted loudly.

46
00:02:35.438 --> 00:02:37.779
"Take the sails down!"

47
00:02:38.200 --> 00:02:41.002
Polynesia was untying the ropes with her beak.

48
00:02:41.503 --> 00:02:42.664
"Where is Charles?"

49
00:02:43.284 --> 00:02:44.005
she screeched.

50
00:02:44.025 --> 00:02:46.527
"Still asleep!"

51
00:02:46.867 --> 00:02:47.908
Tommy yelled back.

52
00:02:48.769 --> 00:02:50.630
Polynesia was very upset.

53
00:02:51.671 --> 00:02:54.313
She flew down to the cabin to wake Charles up.

54
00:02:54.333 --> 00:02:55.214
"Get up!

55
00:02:55.554 --> 00:02:56.255
Get up!"

56
00:02:56.755 --> 00:02:57.256
she yelled.

57
00:02:58.324 --> 00:03:00.285
She pecked him on the nose and forehead.

58
00:03:01.045 --> 00:03:03.165
And she pulled his ears─hard!

59
00:03:03.185 --> 00:03:06.266
"Ouch!" He jumped up out of bed.

60
00:03:09.307 --> 00:03:11.688
The wind tossed the boat this way and that.

61
00:03:12.148 --> 00:03:15.189
The wheel spun out of control, knocking Dr.

62
00:03:15.209 --> 00:03:16.369
Dolittle to the floor.

63
00:03:16.969 --> 00:03:20.690
As for poor Tommy, he could not get the sails off by himself.

64
00:03:21.330 --> 00:03:25.631
In fact, the wind was so strong that it lifted him off his feet!

65
00:03:25.651 --> 00:03:27.552
"Hang on tightly!"

66
00:03:28.084 --> 00:03:29.385
Dr. Dolittle shouted.

67
00:03:31.247 --> 00:03:32.808
Charles ran onto the deck.

68
00:03:33.248 --> 00:03:35.050
The rain beat against his face.

69
00:03:35.650 --> 00:03:37.712
"That hurts more than Polynesia's pecking!"

70
00:03:38.092 --> 00:03:38.633
he cried.

71
00:03:39.333 --> 00:03:43.877
Charles was a big strong man, but even he could not get the sails down.

72
00:03:43.897 --> 00:03:46.579
"The wind is blowing too hard," he yelled.

73
00:03:48.681 --> 00:03:51.703
Tommy was never so frightened in his whole life.

74
00:03:51.843 --> 00:03:53.685
But he knew he must help Charles.

75
00:03:53.705 --> 00:03:55.366
"The sail is stuck!"

76
00:03:55.906 --> 00:03:57.608
Polynesia was saying to Charles.

77
00:03:58.156 --> 00:04:00.238
"Tommy! Can you climb up the mast?"

78
00:04:00.578 --> 00:04:01.218
she shouted.

79
00:04:02.839 --> 00:04:03.740
Tommy looked up.

80
00:04:04.240 --> 00:04:05.982
The mast was awfully high up.

81
00:04:06.422 --> 00:04:08.063
But he knew he had to do it.

82
00:04:08.083 --> 00:04:10.165
"Yes," he answered.

83
00:04:10.605 --> 00:04:12.987
Then he started to climb up the thick pole.

84
00:04:15.008 --> 00:04:16.189
Tommy reached the top.

85
00:04:16.669 --> 00:04:18.911
One of the sails was caught between the ropes.

86
00:04:19.531 --> 00:04:21.973
That's why they weren't able to pull the sails down.

87
00:04:22.534 --> 00:04:25.536
Tommy used all his strength and pulled the sail loose.

88
00:04:26.192 --> 00:04:30.475
As it fell onto the boat, he heard Charles and Polynesia yelling up at him.

89
00:04:32.376 --> 00:04:36.039
Tommy turned his head and saw a huge wave coming toward him.

90
00:04:36.699 --> 00:04:38.580
There was no time to climb down.

91
00:04:39.201 --> 00:04:42.163
He closed his eyes and held tightly to the mast.

92
00:04:42.683 --> 00:04:45.305
He thought about his mother and father in Puddleby.

93
00:04:45.845 --> 00:04:47.726
Then everything went black.
